s9-p2 = prose (cons "Having represented a language's meaning and a machine's transitions, the next question is not whether both can be called programs, but what relation makes the machine's behavior a realization of the source. The answer must be an explicit simulation or refinement relating the actual observations of the two. Hoare logic, compiler correctness, and verified source-to-machine refinement have extensive prior art ([17](#ref-17), [18](#ref-18), [22](#ref-22)). LLVM provides an influential reusable intermediate representation and transformation infrastructure ([30](#ref-30)). The examples here formulate source and target machines and their correspondence as terms and proofs. The implementation route is C followed by an existing C compiler (§9.4). The small decoded machine below exposes the compositional argument; it does not prescribe a new instruction-set backend." nil)
